# Findings the image scan may report that this service is not exposed to. Each line states why, and
# nothing goes in here without one.

# GHSA-r277-6w6q-xmqw — kin-openapi: ValidationHandler.Load() fails open, fixed in 0.144.0.
#
# Trivy finds v0.140.0 inside usr/local/bin/frankenphp, not in a package this image installs: it is
# vendored into the FrankenPHP binary, which bundles Caddy and its modules. There is nothing to
# upgrade — the base is pinned to dunglas/frankenphp:php8.5, and that digest is still what the tag
# resolves to today, so upstream has not rebuilt with the patched library.
#
# The vulnerable code is Caddy's OpenAPI validation handler. This container never configures it:
# there is no Caddyfile in the repository, no openapi setting in config/, and the image starts with
# `php artisan octane:start`, which serves PHP and nothing else. A handler that is never loaded
# cannot fail open.
#
# Revisit when dunglas/frankenphp publishes a build carrying kin-openapi 0.144.0 or newer; then this
# line goes away rather than being renewed.
GHSA-r277-6w6q-xmqw
